ONE EXCEPTION, RESERVED: server/

Server-side deployment code under server/ is NOT covered by this license and is
all rights reserved. It is the one component that could be cloned into a hosted
competitor, so it starts closed. Loosening a license later is trivial; tightening
one is impossible, which is the only reason for the asymmetry.

Everything the server needs in order to be useful -- the data, the schemas, the
skills, the client, the importers -- is MIT or CC0, so a fork can host its own
without asking. What is reserved is this deployment, not the capability.
